{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>That your ox and your donkey may rest.</b> Its explanation: for this reason your ox and your donkey may rest — that is, the commandment of Sabbath, that you should work six and rest on the seventh, is for this reason — that your ox and your donkey and the son of your handmaid and the stranger may rest. For the intent of the verse concerning the Sabbath commandment is not so that the ox and the donkey may rest; and similar to it (Deuteronomy 16:3): למען תזכור את יום צאתך מארץ מצרים, whose explanation is: for this reason you shall remember the day of your going out."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:15.792425652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}